{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-gal-2-1","title":"Galatians 2:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GAL","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 He shows when he went up again to Jerusalem, and for what purpose; 3 and that Titus was not circumcised; 11 and that he resisted Peter, and told him the reason; 14 why he and others, being Jews, do believe in Christ to be justified by faith, and not by works; 20 and that they live not in sin, who are so justified.</p>\n<p>fourteen. 1:18 I went. Ac 15:2-4 Barnabas. 13; Ac 4:36,37; 11:25,30; 12:25; 13:2,50; 14:12; 15:25,36-39; 1Co 9:6 Col 4:10 Titus. 3; 2Co 8:16,23; Tit 1:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gal-2-2","title":"Galatians 2:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GAL","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>by. Ac 16:9,10; 18:9; 23:11 communicated. 9; 1:16; Ac 15:4,12; 1Co 1:23; 2:2 privately. or, severally. which. 6,9; Ec 10:1; Ac 5:34; Php 2:29 I should. Mt 10:16; 1Co 9:26; Php 2:16; 1Th 3:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gal-2-3","title":"Galatians 2:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GAL","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>5:2-6; Ac 15:24; 16:3; 1Co 9:20,21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gal-2-4","title":"Galatians 2:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GAL","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>because. 5:10,12; Ac 15:1,24; 20:30; 2Co 11:13,17,26; 1Jo 4:1 unawares. 2Ti 3:6; 2Pe 2:1,2; Jude 1:4 liberty. 3:23-26; 5:1,13; Ps 51:12; 119:45; Joh 8:31-36; 2Co 3:17; 1Pe 2:16 2Pe 2:19 bring. 4:3,9,10,25; Isa 51:23; 2Co 11:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gal-2-5","title":"Galatians 2:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"GAL","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>we. 3:1,2; Ac 15:2; Col 2:4-8; Jude 1:3 that. 14; 4:16; Eph 1:13; Col 1:5; 1Th 2:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-gal-2-6","title":"Galatians 2:6","author":